CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ deduced from indices<I\.\.\.>: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
The concept-aware parse of a template parameter beginning with a
qualified name did not declare the parameter to the parser's scope, so
`I...' in `indices<I...>' was parsed as a type pack expansion and only
one element was deduced.
